###
# Renew tokens and profile (note: POST /renew/issue was removed)
# Tokens are now issued automatically when a listing is APPROVED by an admin.
# Use the profile endpoint to inspect your user data (includes listings and renewTokens),
# or list tokens directly via the tokens endpoint.

###
# Auth - profile (authenticated)
GET {{host}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# Renew Flow (auto-issued on approval)
# 1. Create a listing (pending)
# 2. Approve listing as ADMIN (see approve endpoint above)
# 3. List renew tokens as the listing owner to obtain the auto-issued token
# 4. Redeem the token to extend expiry
# Notes:
#  - Manual issue & delete endpoints were removed.
#  - Tokens are upserted per approved listing (one active token per listing).
#  - Update / Patch endpoints are ADMIN utilities (e.g., force-expire, mark used).

### 3. Renew - list my tokens (authenticated user)
GET {{host}}/renew/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### (Optional) Renew - list tokens (admin overview)
GET {{host}}/renew/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### (Optional) Renew - get token by id (admin)
GET {{host}}/renew/tokens/{{renewTokenId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### (Optional) Renew - update token (admin)
PUT {{host}}/renew/tokens/{{renewTokenId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "used": true
}

### (Optional) Renew - patch token (admin)
PATCH {{host}}/renew/tokens/{{renewTokenId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expiresAt": "2025-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
}

### 4. Renew - redeem token (authenticated user)
POST {{host}}/renew/redeem
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "PASTE_TOKEN_VALUE_FROM_LIST_STEP",
  "clientIp": "127.0.0.1"
}

